12118	{"artifactId":"LLD-2ff0dfdadb1c8d1c-s5","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-2ff0dfdadb1c8d1c-s5-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-08T16:16:58.718Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"warn","summary":"review: warn","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"warn","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The LLD designs every s5 acceptance criterion in the DEF (ac1 one timestamped read-only snapshot, ac2 deterministic order and counts, ac3 marker-less build evidence through the daemon, ac4 1,000 records / 500 items within budget, ac5 existing IPC clients unchanged, ac6 shape fixed and mirrored for three clients).","evidence":"DEF-2ff0dfdadb1c8d1c.json s5 acceptanceCriteria ac1-ac6 (lines 1079-1134) match: §2.1 read-only postconditions + takenAt (ac1), §2.2 sorted items + deep-equal postcondition (ac2), §2.4 deliveryEvidence returning meta/body/marker-less markdown (ac3), 500 ms edge case (ac4), additive-only exports with existing tests unchanged (ac5), types.ts + vscode mirror + JSON sample (ac6). The DEF functionalRequirements (changes to existing IPC only additive) are respected by §3.3/§3.4.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The snapshot fields the LLD assembles are exactly the HLD sc7 interface sketch (DeliveryItem with attentionReasons typed (AttentionReason | NoticeCode)[], DeliveryEvidenceEntry with mdPath/openWith, DeliverySnapshot with schemaVersion 1, counts, attentionRule; DeliveryEvidenceRecord with meta/body/renderedMarkdown).","evidence":"HLD-2ff0dfdadb1c8d1c.json sc7 interfaceSketch (line 318) lists the same fields, the same error mapping (absent store -> empty snapshot, unreadable -> error, id regex -> 'invalid artifact id', missing -> 'not found'), and the same response unions.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"handleWorkflowPending takes (params, repoEnv), resolves repo from non-empty params.repo else repoEnv, and returns { error: 'workflow.pending: `repo` is required' } — the idiom the new handlers copy.","evidence":"src/workflow/pending.ts:67-80: `export function handleWorkflowPending(params: { repo?: string } | undefined, repoEnv: string | undefined)` ... `if (repoPath.length === 0) return { error: 'workflow.pending: `repo` is required' }` with a try/catch mapping to `workflow.pending: ${message}`.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"handleArtifactContent today holds an inline lexical-plus-realpath docs/ containment check that can be extracted into resolveDocsMarkdown with the same error messages.","evidence":"src/workflow/artifact-content.ts:114-154: lexical `relative(docsRoot, absMd)` check, `.md` check, `realpathSync(absMd)` / `realpathSync(docsRoot)` with 'resolves outside docs/ via a symlink' error, then readFileSync. All messages are prefixed 'workflow.artifactContent:' and include p.mdPath, so the extracted helper must take the caller's prefix/mdPath to keep them word for word, as the LLD's test requires.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Real BUILD records stamp no epicSlug or epicCreatedAt (BUILD-2ff0dfdadb1c8d1c-s1 has only epicHash, storyId, createdAt), so meta-based md-path derivation cannot locate them.","evidence":".insrc/artifacts/BUILD-2ff0dfdadb1c8d1c-s1.json meta: workflow, epicHash, storyId 's1', createdAt, updatedAt, authoredBy, approvedAt — no epicSlug/epicCreatedAt. pending.ts:187-198 deriveMdPath falls back to meta.createdAt and slug=hash, which would give a wrong folder; hence the graph + listWorkItems lookup.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The reused delivery functions exist with the stated shapes: loadArtifactRecordSet(repo, fs?, now?), liftStoreFile(fileName, parsed) -> ArtifactRecord | RecordLoadFailure, buildWorkItemGraph(recordSet), deriveStages/deriveGates/deriveCurrency(graph, recordSet), makeNotice, sortNotices, DeliveryStoreUnreadableError.","evidence":"load.ts:63 liftStoreFile, :111 loadArtifactRecordSet(repoPath, fs = nodeStoreFs, now) throwing DeliveryStoreUnreadableError when listDir fails and returning an empty set when the dir is absent; graph.ts:191 buildWorkItemGraph; stage.ts:239, gate.ts:362, currency.ts:295 each (graph, recordSet); notice.ts:44 makeNotice, :73 sortNotices; types.ts:278 DeliveryStoreUnreadableError.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"deriveMdPath is a private function in pending.ts taking PendingKind, and widening it to path-scheme's ArtifactKind is additive; listWorkItems exists and lists docs/epics and docs/standalone folders.","evidence":"pending.ts:187 `function deriveMdPath(repoPath, kind: PendingKind, meta)` (not exported) already casts `kind as ArtifactKind`; PENDING_KINDS (SPEC, DEF, HLD, LLD, PLAN, ISSUE, CR) ⊂ ArtifactKind (path-scheme.ts:46). path-scheme.ts:201 listWorkItems returns { kind, root: 'docs/<top>/<name>' } — repo-relative, so the port must join it with repoPath to report an absolute mdPath as the LLD states. ArtifactKind has no AMD, consistent with AMD -> null.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.3","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The sc7 types and new modules (snapshot.ts, handlers.ts, the two IPC methods) do not already exist.","evidence":"Glob src/workflow/delivery/**/*.ts lists notice, stage, read, load, gate, graph, types, currency only; types.ts has no Delivery* sc7 types; src/daemon/index.ts has 'workflow.pending' (686) and 'workflow.artifactContent' (698) but no 'workflow.delivery'.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The daemon handler map registers workflow.* methods as lazy-import closures passing (params, process.env['INSRC_REPO']), so two new entries beside 'workflow.pending' are the complete daemon change.","evidence":"src/daemon/index.ts:686-703: `'workflow.pending': async (params) => { const { handleWorkflowPending } = await import('../workflow/pending.js'); return handleWorkflowPending(params as ..., process.env['INSRC_REPO']); }` and the same shape for 'workflow.artifactContent'.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The VS Code mirror can import src/workflow/delivery/types.ts by relative path and type-check under the plugin's tsconfig, as docs-review-client imports pending.ts.","evidence":"vscode-plugin/tsconfig.json: nodenext, strict, exactOptionalPropertyTypes, noEmit, include 'src/**/*.ts' (so delivery-contract.ts is also covered by the existing build, not only by the new tsconfig.delivery-contract.json). types.ts imports only '../review/types.js', which has no imports itself, and stays type-only apart from DeliveryStoreUnreadableError.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Older and flat stored shapes are handled: flat AMD records lift as meta (all top-level fields but amendment) + body (amendment), and marker-less BUILD.md files remain readable through deliveryEvidence.","evidence":"load.ts:70-83 liftStoreFile for AMD: `const { amendment, ...meta } = top; ... meta, body: amendment`. The LLD reuses liftStoreFile and returns marker-less markdown with openWith 'evidence-read'. No stored shape is written or migrated (read-only), and schemaVersion 1 versions the published shape per HLD sc7.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The LLD stays inside s5: it consumes sc1-sc6 without re-deriving identity, routes, gates or currency, and the build-without-plan completeness notice it adds is the half s4's boundary hands to s5.","evidence":"s4 boundary text: 'the build-without-plan half is tested in s5'; NoticeCode in types.ts:127 already declares `'incomplete-evidence' // s4 / s5`. The LLD reads routes from sc4 StageAnnotation.route, attention reasons from sc5 ItemGates, currency/amendments from sc6, and only merges notices via makeNotice/sortNotices.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"An absent store yields an empty snapshot while an unlistable store is detectable as a thrown DeliveryStoreUnreadableError that the handler maps to { error }.","evidence":"load.ts:118 `if (!fs.exists(dir)) return { repo, readAt, records: [], failures: [] }`; :121-125 listDir failure throws `new DeliveryStoreUnreadableError(dir, ...)` whose message names the store path (types.ts:282).","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The deliveryEvidence id pattern admits every real artifact id shape, including AMD-<hash>-<n> and story-suffixed ids, while excluding separators and '..'.","evidence":"Pattern ^(SPEC|DEF|HLD|LLD|PLAN|BUILD|CR|ISSUE|EXT|AMD)-[0-9a-f]{16}(-[A-Za-z0-9]+)?$ matches 'BUILD-2ff0dfdadb1c8d1c-s1', 'DEF-2ff0dfdadb1c8d1c', and 'AMD-<hash>-1' (EffectiveAmendment.amendmentId doc in types.ts:249); the suffix class has no '/', '.' or '\\'. Identical to the HLD sc7 error-path sketch.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each ac maps to a named test, and the ac4 fixture really yields 1,000 records and 500 work items; the ac5 regression tests exist.","evidence":"§6 acceptance mapping covers ac1-ac6. Fixture arithmetic: 100 epics × (DEF+HLD) = 200 records + 400 stories × (LLD+PLAN) = 800 records = 1,000; items 100 epics + 400 stories = 500 (empty-task PLANs mint no task items). src/workflow/__tests__/pending.test.ts and artifact-content.test.ts exist for the 'unchanged' ac5 mapping.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.2","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The 500 ms budget for ac4 can be met with the real markdown port (one listWorkItems plus up to 1,000 realpath + 512-byte reads) on the reference environment.","evidence":"No benchmark of loadArtifactRecordSet + the four passes + per-record realpath/read exists in the repo to compare against; the DEF says only 'the agreed time budget', and I did not find where 500 ms was agreed. Timing depends on the machine running the test.","action":"Confirm 500 ms is the agreed k6 budget, and keep the best-of-three timing so the test is not flaky on slow CI.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":16,"unverified":1},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-08T16:16:58.718Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
